  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Offer Tailoring and embroidery skills to 100 Women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Education Statistics 2016 and Management Information System (EMIS), show that 73% of men and 84% of women above 15 years of age are illiterate with 3 out of 5 school-aged children not enrolled in primary school, and the teacher -pupil ratio averaging 48.154 per teacher. Vocational training and offering livelihood skills to the youth and women can change the population economic situation. CSD is on the struggle to build the capacities of young women for business purposes.</narrative>
  </description>
